            <value>0</value>
          </lowerValue>
          <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm.DefinedTerm.inDefinedTermSet.upper" xmi:uuid="8f2b0379-734e-53d7-a100-659615f6d817">
            <value>1</value>
          </upperValue>
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm.DefinedTerm.inDefinedTermSet.comment" xmi:uuid="ca7766cd-19c4-5c43-9420-62f17320f4e1">
            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

The controlled vocabulary responsible for this keyword, as EITHER a plain URI string identifying the vocabulary, OR an object reference ({"@id": "&lt;uri&gt;"}) to a vocabulary defined elsewhere in the document. Both forms are already in use across CDIF profiles and downstream ADA building blocks; permitting only the string form made the object form - the natural JSON-LD spelling of a reference - invalid, while this class's own union-type policy above explicitly anticipates both.</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm.DefinedTerm.inDefinedTermSet"/>
          </ownedComment>
        </ownedAttribute>
